# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reclaim environment
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS OPTIONAL. With this file empty, the app runs end to end
# on local adapters: embedded Postgres, in-process locks, deterministic copy,
# and a payments simulator that signs its own webhooks.
#
# Each variable below UPGRADES one local adapter to a real service. The boot
# banner prints which adapter is active for every port, so nothing is hidden.
# Setup steps for each: docs/SETUP.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset      -> PGlite, embedded Postgres at .data/pglite. No Docker needed.
# Set        -> any Postgres. Docker Compose locally, or a Supabase POOLER URI.
#               Use the pooler (port 6543), not the direct connection: the free
#               tier allows 60 direct connections but 200 through the pooler.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:6543/postgres
#
# DB_POOL_MAX default is 20 (node-pg's own library default, 10, was measured as
# the real bottleneck under concurrent load — see docs/LOAD_TEST.md). Raise it
# if your Postgres allows more real concurrent connections than that.
# DB_POOL_MAX=20

# ── Lock and counter store ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset      -> Postgres-backed. Durable, shared across processes, zero setup.
# Set        -> Upstash Redis over REST.
# Note: the KV store is NEVER the idempotency authority. That is a UNIQUE
# constraint inside the same transaction as the write. See BUILD_PLAN.md 5.1.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Language model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset      -> deterministic template engine, including a Hinglish variant.
# Set        -> Groq. Free tier is 30 req/min, 8k tokens/min, 200k tokens/day,
#               so batch runs stay template-first and sample the model. The
#               budget guard sits deliberately below those limits.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# ── Payments provider ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset      -> simulator. Signs its own webhooks through the same HMAC path.
# Set        -> Razorpay TEST MODE. Never live keys; the app refuses rzp_live_.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxx
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
#
# The webhook secret is a SEPARATE value from the API key secret above. You
# invent it when creating the webhook in the Razorpay dashboard. Mixing these
# two up makes every delivery return 400 with no other symptom.
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Executor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dry_run (default) records exactly what WOULD have been sent, and touches no
# network. Batch replays are always dry_run regardless of this setting, which
# is how a 300-event batch can never exhaust the 30-Payment-Link test cap.
# EXECUTOR_MODE=dry_run
# EXECUTOR_LIVE_BUDGET=5

# ── Explicit adapter overrides (normally unnecessary) ───────────────────────
# DB_DRIVER=pglite|postgres
# KV_DRIVER=memory|postgres|upstash
# LLM_DRIVER=template|groq
# PAYMENTS_DRIVER=simulator|razorpay

# ── Public-instance posture ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this on any deployment reachable from the open internet. It does not add
# authentication (there is none — see SECURITY.md); it removes two things that
# are fine locally and are reconnaissance on a public URL:
#
#   1. /api/health stops publishing each port's `target`, which on a configured
#      instance names a real database host and a real Upstash host. Adapter
#      names, live flags, and the human-readable `reason` still come through.
#   2. /api/dev/* stops responding at all (404). Those routes exist so
#      scripts/replay.ts and scripts/burst.ts never open a second connection to
#      a single-process embedded database; they are unauthenticated, and before
#      this flag nothing but the word "dev" in the path stopped them answering
#      in a production build.
#
# Deliberately NOT keyed off NODE_ENV: the documented local demo path runs a
# real production build, so gating on NODE_ENV would break the demo this flag
# exists to protect. It is an explicit deployment choice.
# RECLAIM_PUBLIC_INSTANCE=1

# ── Real message delivery (opt-in, one consented recipient) ─────────────────
# The language layer always drafts a real recovery message; without one of these
# it is thrown away, because every customer in every scenario here is synthetic
# and this project does not send unsolicited messages to real addresses.
#
# Set one or both to prove delivery against an address you own. Payment Links
# will then notify that recipient for real, and Razorpay records a real delivery.
# Absent (the default) means no notification and no contact detail is sent at all.
# RECLAIM_NOTIFY_EMAIL=you@example.com
# RECLAIM_NOTIFY_CONTACT=+919876543210
